Subject: [PATCH] qemu: avoid closing the shared wait channel while configuring usernet

QEMU's wait goroutine and the usernet configuration goroutine both report
startup errors through qWaitCh. Closing qWaitCh from the QEMU wait goroutine
allows the usernet goroutine to panic when it reports an error after QEMU
exits.

Keep room for both results and leave the channel open. The caller only needs
the first error, while both producers can finish without a send-on-closed-
channel panic.

---
 pkg/driver/qemu/qemu_driver.go | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu_driver.go b/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu_driver.go
--- a/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu_driver.go
+++ b/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu_driver.go
@@ -553,9 +553,10 @@
 	}
 	l.qCmd = qCmd
-	l.qWaitCh = make(chan error, 1)
+	// Both QEMU's wait goroutine and the network configuration goroutine may
+	// report an error. Keep room for both and do not close the channel from one
+	// producer while the other can still send.
+	l.qWaitCh = make(chan error, 2)
 	go func() {
-		defer close(l.qWaitCh)
 		defer cancel()
 		err := qCmd.Wait()
